    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d783">

                <pb facs="0907" n="827" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg827"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Clayton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-11-17"><hi rendition="#italic">November 17,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 803.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 1614 of the 24th ultimo on the subject of jurisdiction by consular
                    officers of the United States in Mexico over disputes arising at sea or in
                    Mexican ports among masters, officers, and crews of American vessels.</p>
                <p>With your dispatch is transmitted a copy of a note from the Mexican minister for
                    foreign affairs, in which he expresses the opinion that a new treaty is not
                    necessary, as without it, and simply by virtue of Mexican laws, the American
                    merchant marine enjoys in Mexican ports all the facilities and exemptions asked
                    for in your note to him of August 14 last.</p>
                <p>In reply, I inclose herewith for your information a copy of the Department’s
                    circular instruction of the 11th instant to our consuls in Mexico, defining
                    their rights and powers in the premises.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d783-a1.xml" xpointer="d783-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
